---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ArrowRight, Bot, SlidersHorizontal, Blocks, GitBranch, PanelRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import {apps} from '../lib/apps';
---
<Base title="From setup to software" description="Let your agent prepare the environment before an idea, configure structured applications, connect independent mini-apps and deploy software you own on Cloudflare.">
 <section class="composer-home-hero"><div><h1>Make software.<br/>Keep it yours.</h1><p class="lede">App Composer helps your coding agent build applications with EmDash and Cloudflare. EmDash gives you content editing and admin; Cloudflare runs the app and stores its data. Get Ready prepares the environment, Init captures your choices, and mini-app APIs connect the useful pieces.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/ready">Start with Get Ready <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a><a class="button secondary" href="/architecture">See the whole platform</a></div><p class="small">Explore here in your browser. Build with your authorised agent, GitHub source and selected Cloudflare account. Public browsing needs no Composer account.</p></div><figure class="home-identity"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/brand/share-composer-20261014-v2-600.webp 600w, /brand/share-composer-20261014-v2.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) calc(100vw - 48px), 540px"/><img src="/brand/share-composer-20261014-v2.jpg" alt="App Composer: From setup to software. A form, a coastal photo and a collection joined by an orange route." width="1200" height="630" fetchpriority="high"/></picture><figcaption>An illustrated view of the photo-to-collection workflow.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <section class="home-process" aria-labelledby="process-heading"><h2 id="process-heading">Start wherever you are.</h2><div class="home-process-row"><Bot size={26} aria-hidden="true"/><div><h3>Before the idea</h3><p>Get Ready prepares the actual tools, GitHub source and Cloudflare connection. Your agent finishes by proving a live HTTPS app.</p></div><a href="/ready">Prepare the environment <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a></div><div class="home-process-row"><SlidersHorizontal size={26} aria-hidden="true"/><div><h3>When you know what you want</h3><p>Init gives the idea structure: apps, fields, appearance, content and deployment intent. Keep a portable spec and the matching agent request.</p></div><a href="/init">Configure an app <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a></div><div class="home-process-row"><Blocks size={26} aria-hidden="true"/><div><h3>When pieces should work together</h3><p>Compose independently maintained apps through their data and actions. Each keeps its own source, configuration and update history.</p></div><a href="/demo">Try the connected pair <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a></div></section>
 <section class="home-apps"><div class="home-section-heading"><div><h2>Small apps with a useful purpose.</h2><p>Use a building block on its own, give it your own settings or connect it to another. These are working applications with independent GitHub repositories.</p></div><a href="/apps">Explore all apps <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a></div><div class="home-app-list">{apps.filter(a=>['guestbook','showcase','linkcheck'].includes(a.id)).map(app=><article><a class="home-app-art" href={app.href}><img src={app.image} alt={`${app.name} original app artwork`} width="320" height="320" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></a><div><h3><a href={app.href}>{app.name}</a></h3><p>{app.description}</p><a class="app-open" href={app.href}>Open app <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true"/></a></div></article>)}</div><p class="small">Here / there owns approved photo contributions. Linkarooie can feature them and open the originals. Hide a source and its controlled feature disappears.</p></section>
 <section class="home-process" id="platform-choices"><h2>Content, cloud and commerce: know what each part does.</h2><p>For an editable website, start with EmDash’s content types, forms and media. Add an independent mini-app when it earns its place. Apps can own separate databases and file storage while presenting one connected experience.</p><div class="home-fit"><div><h3>Coming from WordPress?</h3><p>Keep the useful content and field workflows familiar from ACF and MetaBox. EmDash provides the editor; an agent builds the application around it. Existing WordPress themes and plugins need an individual fit check.</p></div><div><h3>Running a shop?</h3><p>Shopify can own commerce and checkout; Stripe can collect payments for a custom app; Printful can fulfil printed products. Those Composer connectors are future work. Replacing WooCommerce requires an order and operations plan, not just a payment button.</p></div></div><p>Cloudflare is the current supported cloud. AWS is a valid infrastructure choice with a different setup; no AWS Composer adapter is verified. Email, customer accounts, costs and recovery also need explicit owners.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/guide">Choose your CMS, cloud and business services <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a></section>
 <section class="home-process"><h2>Use the admin to do the everyday work.</h2><p>Invited administrators can manage the photo pair from EmDash: upload and approve a photo, feature it in Linkarooie, publish a draft link and change each app’s appearance. Records stay in the app that owns them; private owner credentials stay on the server.</p><p>The native catalogue editor and media library remain part of EmDash. A tailored admin for every customer app is still work to deliver.</p><a href="/guide#admin-screenshots">See the working admin screenshots</a> · <a href="/_emdash/admin/plugins/composer-miniapps/apps">Open owner administration</a></section>
 <section class="home-platform"><div><PanelRight size={26} aria-hidden="true"/><h2>Built around the way you work.</h2><p>Get Ready is an independent library, local API and optional MCP—not just a website checklist. The optional Chrome extension brings the same workspace into the Cloudflare dashboard. Structured Init forms carry your intent to the agent.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/architecture">Understand the parts and their status <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true"/></a></div><div><GitBranch size={26} aria-hidden="true"/><h2>Your source.<br/>Your next move.</h2><p>Woodhouse operates implementation without becoming a customer runtime dependency. Your apps keep their independent source, configuration and data. An update must preserve the work you made.</p><p class="small">The working operator path is live. Fresh-account onboarding, customer-deployed content forms and dashboard installation acceptance remain active work.</p><a href="/release">Read what is verified</a> · <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer">Inspect the source</a></div></section>
</Base>
<style>
.home-fit{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;margin:28px 0}.home-fit h3{font-size:1.4rem;margin:0 0 12px}.home-fit p{font-size:16px;color:var(--color-muted)}@media(max-width:700px){.home-fit{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}}
 .composer-home-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:56px;align-items:center;padding:12px 0 56px}.composer-home-hero h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,5.8vw,5rem);max-width:18ch;margin-top:0}.composer-home-hero .lede{font-size:1.16rem;max-width:56ch}.home-identity img{display:block;width:100%;border-radius:8px}.home-identity figcaption{font-size:13px;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:12px}.home-process,.home-apps,.home-platform{border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);padding:40px 0;margin-top:24px}.home-process h2,.home-apps h2,.home-platform h2{font-size:2.1rem;margin-bottom:20px;max-width:26ch}.home-process-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:32px minmax(0,1fr) 230px;gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border);padding:24px 0;align-items:start}.home-process-row>svg{color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:3px}.home-process-row h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin:0 0 8px}.home-process-row p{margin:0;color:var(--color-muted);font-size:15px;max-width:65ch}.home-process-row>a,.home-section-heading>a,.app-open{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:44px;font-size:14px}.home-section-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start}.home-section-heading p{margin:0;color:var(--color-muted);max-width:70ch}.home-section-heading>a{white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0}.home-app-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:40px;margin-top:32px}.home-app-list article{display:flex;gap:18px}.home-app-art{width:88px;flex-shrink:0}.home-app-art img{display:block;width:100%;border-radius:8px;aspect-ratio:1}.home-app-list h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin:0 0 10px}.home-app-list h3 a{text-decoration:none}.home-app-list p{margin:0;color:var(--color-muted);font-size:14px}.app-open{margin-top:8px}.home-platform{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:64px}.home-platform svg{color:var(--color-muted);margin-bottom:20px}.home-platform .button svg{margin:0}.home-platform p{color:var(--color-muted)}
 @media(max-width:1100px){.home-app-list{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.home-app-list article{max-width:650px}.home-app-art{width:110px}}
 @media(max-width:800px){.composer-home-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:28px}.composer-home-hero h1{font-size:3rem}.home-identity{max-width:600px}.home-process-row{grid-template-columns:28px 1fr;gap:16px}.home-process-row>a{grid-column:2}.home-section-heading{display:block}.home-section-heading>a{margin-top:16px}.home-platform{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:36px}.home-process h2,.home-apps h2,.home-platform h2{font-size:1.85rem}.home-app-art{width:88px}}
</style>
